construction-ID cache. The pinned source is EnergyPlus 26.1.0 commit
`6f2e40d10250a105b49966baa24d843711e61048`. Construction.cc 146-165 resets all
twelve public 19-slot arrays, metadata and UValue before the unused return. A used
construction assigns caller TimeStepZone at194; shared loading ErrorsFound causes
the return at313-315. Those are genuine reset/early-return states, not generated
coefficient successes. CON01's excluded construction/material/source routes stay
excluded and must have explicit unavailable owners.

For a reached massive no-source 1D route, common stores at1024-1077 consume the
last actual private s0/s/e and current converted conductance cnd. NumCTFTerms is
that private method's term count. CTFTimeStep and NumHistories are the caller's
postcheck members, which can differ from the last method stamp after a severe
seven-hour break. Unary negation precedes multiplication by the unchanged CFU
expression. Flux[0] remains its reset positive zero. Source/sink arrays and all
untouched tails retain their reset bits. No SI resistance sum substitutes cnd.

The all-resistive branch985-1018 is already owned by CTF02. The proposed adapter
copies that actual owner; it does not recalculate the branch or its coefficients.
The standalone massive copier does not decide whether stores were reached. Its
future caller must first establish the actual selected terminal route. Fatal939
