## Reverse reuse and ordered Init

Reverse selection405-485 occurs only on the massive side of the literal predicate
LayersInConstruct > NumResLayers. It scans actual earlier Construct elements up to
the current address. The first equal-length reversed original LayerPoint ID stack
whose earlier construction IsUsedCTF is true wins. It does not compare normalized
layers, material values, cache hashes, or numerical coefficient equality. There
is no separate generic duplicate rule; a palindrome can match this same rule.

Reverse storage460-475 copies earlier public timestep/history/term count, swaps
inside/outside, copies cross, and copies flux only for indices1..NumCTFTerms.
Current Flux[0] remains reset. Current UValue still becomes current cnd*CFU at1077;
it is not copied from the earlier UValue. The earlier public owner must exist even
when its real earlier call returned a reset/error state. Missing custody is an
unavailable join, never an invented zero or successful generated owner.

InitConductionTransferFunctions6153-6202 owns one ErrorsFound=false and one
DoCTFErrorReport=false across all actual Construct elements in declaration order.
After each whole call returns, it updates SimpleCTFOnly from NumHistories and the
maximum public NumCTFTerms. Then AnyInternalHeatSourceInInput can clear SimpleCTFOnly.
Used constructions report layers; ScanForReports and DoCTFErrorReport select the
coefficient reports; final shared ErrorsFound throws only after these reports.
A fatal inside a construction bypasses that call's aggregate updates and all
later Init work. Source-returned, fatal-unwound, and observer failure are distinct.

## Fixed public capacity

Construction.hh declares std::array<Real64,19>; valid indices are0..18. The
inclusive stores and reverse copies use NumCTFTerms without a capacity check.
The09 severe break can retain a larger term count before those stores. This is a
source-derived unchecked-access risk, not an observed crash or a fixture to
manufacture. No clamp, relaxed profile, or invented Native error resolves it.

The standalone module returns a typed unrepresentable-input result outside its
within-capacity contract. That result is a Rust interface limitation, not a Native
branch/outcome. Future observations must retain the actual Native whole outcome
and any safe fixed-array postreturn copy independently; no return or safe store is
inferred from a retry LoopExit. Ordinary admitted cases need genuine observations
before a broader capacity or public-store conclusion.

